    "title": "Rate-half distance-three bounded-tail dihedral row codegree",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "If all but t exceptional pairs are orbits of one antipodal or constant-product involution, every nonidentical outside involution orbit has normalized-row codegree at most t, while at most one orbit has identical normalized rows. In the official degree-two quartic-support branch t is at most 40; extending the trace-collision exclusion to the resulting degree-(e+t) complements remains open.",
